WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.518
(soft piano music)

00:00:02.518 --> 00:00:03.916
- [Narrator] This incredible glacier,

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:07.896
located in Alaska, is a
popular tourist destination.

00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:11.117
But the best way to see
it is from the inside.

00:00:11.117 --> 00:00:14.713
(soft piano music)

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:17.847
Mendenhall Glacier is
a 12-mile long glacier

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:19.025
in the Mendenhall Valley

00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:22.105
in Alaska's Tongass National Forest.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:26.188
The ice caves are the
glacier's surreal interior.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.465
Access to see these icy walls

00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:33.219
are only available to
the truly adventurous.

00:00:33.219 --> 00:00:35.922
To see the ice caves
requires a kayak trip,

00:00:35.922 --> 00:00:37.979
an ice climb over the glacier,

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:39.980
and once you're inside, the faith

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.147
that the melting walls
around you won't give away.

00:00:45.018 --> 00:00:48.494
But this natural wonder is under threat.

00:00:48.494 --> 00:00:49.892
The glacier has been retreating

00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:52.147
incredibly quickly in recent years

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:55.660
due to warmer temperatures
and rising sea levels.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.493
It has receded by almost
two miles since 1958.

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:04.866
But what remains is an utterly
breathtaking fantasy land.

00:01:04.866 --> 00:01:07.783
(soft piano music)

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.750
(techno beep)

